{"type":"message","id":"d3d98b36","parentId":"3add4099","timestamp":"2026-03-16T09:58:16.698Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Sender (untrusted metadata):\n```json\n{\n  \"label\": \"openclaw-control-ui\",\n  \"id\": \"openclaw-control-ui\"\n}\n```\n\n[Mon 2026-03-16 09:58 UTC] I need you to modify kidney cancer detection, according to this logic:\n- Do not use anymore the static image path. Before actually running the kidney cancer detection, you have to upload the image, using the following URL:\n\"http://looporchestra.sytes.net:4001/nodes/input/upload?storage_ref=nodes_bucket&local_file_path=upload%2F&user_id=626130f7c71f6b9e651c76be\". Leave the \"storage_ref \"and \"local_file_path\" static as they are, while replacing the \"user_id\" with the telegram user id. The actual image you have to upload needs to be sent opening the image in RB e sending it as POST multipart/form-data in the request.\n\nA response example given by that URL call is attached below. \n {\n “path”: “upload/2026-03-15_14.52.42_5EdSbYnzCrKdhainPvGx/“,\n “filename”: “9dd106ff-65ad-4a16-a381-6d76e4845c9c.jpg”,\n “column_names”: null\n }\n]\n\nEssentially, after uploading the image through this url, you refer to the image path by merging \"path\" + \"filename\", getting your new image_path, that will be the one used to recall the kidney cancer detection inference.\nPerform this modification. If anything is unclear, ask before proceeding"}],"timestamp":1773655096694}}
